cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "experimentation: a conversational journey from coin tosses to causal handoff"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Monfared
    given-names: Khazhak
    alias: k1monfared
abstract: >-
  A nineteen-chapter inquiry-based walkthrough of statistical experimentation,
  paired with the expkit Python library and a small interactive playground.
  Frequentist and Bayesian (PyMC) lenses run side by side in every chapter,
  from "is this coin fair" through power, the test family, confidence
  intervals, multi-arm A/B tests, segmentation, Simpson's paradox, novelty
  effects, dilution, metric quality, attribution, and a frequentist-vs-
  Bayesian shipping capstone, ending with a handoff to a separate causal
  inference repository.
keywords:
  - statistics
  - experimentation
  - A/B testing
  - Bayesian inference
  - PyMC
  - causal inference
  - hierarchical models
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/k1monfared/experimentation"
